      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "##  🔍Teacher Notes\r\nAfter learning about about HTTP and DNS, students will spend a few minutes working with AI Chat to connect what they’ve learned to the real-world energy impact of online communication and AI systems.\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #B7E0E5; display: inline-block;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-user-graduate\"></i> Career Journeys\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## AI Chat: Energy Costs of the Internet\r\n\r\nYou are a network analyst investigating how Internet and AI systems use energy.  \r\nEvery time you send an HTTP request—whether you’re loading a webpage, image, or AI model—energy is consumed by servers, data centers, and network hardware that make the Internet work. \r\n\r\nYour task is to explore where that energy is used, why it matters, and how it can be reduced by interacting with a chatbot that can explain these processes.\r\n\r\n### Your Task:\r\n\r\n1. Start a conversation with the chatbot.  \r\n   * Ask questions about how Internet and AI systems consume energy.  \r\n   * Use precise questions to get clear and detailed responses (see sample conversation starters below).  \r\n\r\n2. Investigate and verify.  \r\n   * Ask follow-up questions to clarify or check the AI’s explanations.  \r\n   * Note what surprised you and any new insights about Internet energy use.  \r\n\r\n3. *Optional for PL:* Record your findings.  \r\n   * Use the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1E5L06Gvl-aWufn3FexmjraDZLFtmlzGVO-eJhh-okFM/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.mfedz7mzei4x\" target=\"blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AI Chat: Energy Costs of the Internet</a> activity guide page to answer the reflection questions based on what you learned.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nNeed help getting started or reflecting? Click below to expand some ideas:\r\n\r\n::: details [**Conversation Starters**]\r\n>- *How much energy does it take to send a typical web request?*  \r\n>- *Where does most of that energy get used?*\r\n>- *How does running AI systems like chatbots compare to loading a website in terms of energy usage?*  \r\n>- *What are some ways to reduce these energy costs?*\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**Reflection Questions**]\r\n>- *What did you learn about where energy is used in Internet or AI systems?*  \r\n>- *What part of the process (like servers, data centers, or transmission) seems to use the most energy, and why?*  \r\n>- *What is one challenge in reducing the energy use of Internet and AI systems?*  \r\n>- *Brainstorm one possible solution or improvement for making online systems more energy efficient.*  \r\n:::",
    "display_name": "Maya",
